    "Scouting Notes": "Multi sport athlete. \n Great bat to ball skills. Will be hit over power.\n Does show gap to gap power and surprising opposite field HR power that he is still tapping into.\n Walked a lot at the lower levels, but less in AA. Seems to be a bit more aggressive and this might be part of the trade off.\n Seems like a good lead off candidate in a year or two, especially if the walks return\n Very fast, but not showing up in quite as many stolen bases as I would have expected. \n Hustles hard on everything, will turn some outs into infield singles and some singles into hustle doubles.\n Potential plus defender in center field. Covers a ton of ground, though jumps and routes are still a little iffy. Has already improved since joining the system.\n Arm is better than I expected, and will be more than enough for center field. \n Honestly think he's close to the big leagues. If the Brewers can't find a solid center fielder at the deadline, I wouldn't be opposed to calling Frelick up.\n In 2023 he's close to being up. The bat is much better since returning from the IL and he's playing a good right field as well, likely preparing for that role in MLB",
